{
  "analysis": "I'm at the workspace root. I can see there's a structure with input_data, final_output directories, and a skill_context directory. I need to explore these to understand the task requirements and existing data before setting up the 4-agent pipeline.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace structure to understand what exists: check the input_data directory for raw_market_data.json, examine skill_context for any documentation, and understand the overall structure before creating the agent workspaces.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la input_data/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input_data/raw_market_data.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the raw_market_data.json contains EV sector data with 4 companies (TeslaMotors, BYDGroup, RivianAuto, LucidMotors), market metrics, trends, and risks. Now I need to read the SKILL.md and manifest.json to understand the requirements for setting up the agent pipeline.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md file from skill_context to understand the required skills and constraints for setting up the multi-agent pipeline. Also check manifest.json and references for additional context.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md was truncated. I can see it describes an agent-orchestrator pattern with sub-agents having inbox/, outbox/, workspace/, status.json, and SKILL.md. I need to see the full file and check the references for templates.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md file and check the references directory for templates and examples that will guide how to set up each agent properly.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -200 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md content is being truncated. I need to read the full file and explore the references directory to understand the templates and patterns for setting up the agents.",
  "plan": "Use different approaches to read the full SKILL.md file and check the references directory for agent templates and examples.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -200 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md is 175 lines but output is truncated. I need to read it in chunks and check the references directory for templates.",
  "plan": "Use sed to read the full SKILL.md file in sections, and explore the references directory for agent templates.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,50p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '51,100p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '101,175p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The terminal output is being truncated. I need to use a different method to read the full SKILL.md file and explore the references directory.",
  "plan": "Use cat with redirection to a temp file, then use head/tail to read it in parts. Also check the references directory for templates.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md > /tmp/skill.md && wc -l /tmp/skill.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -80 /tmp/skill.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -100 /tmp/skill.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The terminal is truncating output. I need to read the SKILL.md in smaller chunks and explore the references directory for agent templates.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md file in smaller sections using sed, and check the references directory for templates that will help set up the agents.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '40,80p' /tmp/skill.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '81,120p' /tmp/skill.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '121,175p' /tmp/skill.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the SKILL.md describes the agent orchestration pattern. Each agent needs SKILL.md, inbox/, outbox/, workspace/, and status.json. There's a reference to sub-agent-templates.md. I need to check the references directory for templates.",
  "plan": "Check the references directory for templates, then read the rest of the SKILL.md file. After understanding the patterns, I'll create the 4 agent workspaces.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/sub-agent-templates.md 2>/dev/null || cat skill_context/references/*.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found the sub-agent-templates.md with templates for Research Agent, Code Agent, and more. I need to see the Analysis Agent, Writer Agent, and Review Agent templates since those are relevant to my task (data-collector, analyst, writer, reviewer).",
  "plan": "Read the rest of the sub-agent-templates.md file to get the templates for Analysis, Writer, and Review agents, then start creating the agent workspaces.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/sub-agent-templates.md > /tmp/templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l /tmp/templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '100,200p' /tmp/templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '200,300p' /tmp/templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the Analysis Agent template. I need to continue reading to get the Writer Agent and Review Agent templates which are critical for my pipeline.",
  "plan": "Continue reading the templates file to get the Writer and Review agent templates, then start creating the agent workspaces.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '200,340p' /tmp/templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I now have all the templates I need. I can see the structure for Analysis Agent, Writer Agent, and Review Agent. Now I need to create the 4 agent workspaces: data-collector, analyst, writer, and reviewer. Each needs SKILL.md, inbox/instructions.md, outbox/, workspace/, and status.json.",
  "plan": "Create the directory structure for all 4 agents, then create their SKILL.md files, inbox instructions, and status.json files. The pipeline flow will be: data-collector → analyst → writer → reviewer.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p agents/data-collector/{inbox,outbox,workspace} agents/analyst/{inbox,outbox,workspace} agents/writer/{inbox,outbox,workspace} agents/reviewer/{inbox,outbox,workspace}\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la agents/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la agents/data-collector/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
